--- fn — function combinator utilities for the handl runtime.
---
--- Single source of truth for the `fn` stdlib interface: 25 function
--- combinators covering composition, control flow, collection iteration,
--- and function manipulation. The Rust bridge in `plugin-lib-utils` loads
--- this file via `include_str!`, parses the `cap` declarations for the
--- plugin capability surface, and registers the Rust handls (handlers) in
--- an `OpRegistry` that dispatches each `op` to its native Rust impl.
---
--- All 25 functions are FFI atoms (they manipulate `serde_json::Value`
--- callables via `apply_fn` from `crate::shared` and cannot be expressed
--- as pure handl arrows without losing the exact `TypeMismatch` error
--- messages the tests rely on). The `op`/`handl` declaration form
--- (ADR-0077 Phase 2) declares the interface; the Rust `Function` impls
--- in `ops.rs` provide the logic.
---
--- ## Capability declarations (ADR-0077 Phase 4)
--- fn.pipe — pipe a value through a sequence of functions left-to-right.
--- fn.flow — compose functions left-to-right into a single inlined function.
--- fn.compose — compose functions right-to-left into a single inlined function.
--- fn.fanout — apply a value to each of several functions, collecting results into a list.
--- fn.fanout_fn — lazy fanout: return a function that splits its input across branches.
--- fn.choice — conditional branching: apply one of two functions based on a predicate.
--- fn.apply — apply a function to an array of arguments.
--- fn.map — map a function over a list.
--- fn.filter — filter a list by a predicate.
--- fn.reduce — fold a list with a function and an initial value.
--- fn.flat_map — map a function over a list and flatten the results.
--- fn.find — find the first element of a list satisfying a predicate.
--- fn.some — test whether any element of a list satisfies a predicate.
--- fn.every — test whether all elements of a list satisfy a predicate.
--- fn.group_by — group elements of a list by a key function.
--- fn.partition — split a list into matching and non-matching elements.
--- fn.count_by — count elements of a list grouped by a key function.
--- fn.tap — call a function for its side effect, returning the original value.
--- fn.match — pattern-match a value against a sequence of pattern/handler branches.
--- fn.constantly — return a function that always yields a fixed value.
--- fn.flip — swap the first two parameters of a function.
--- fn.partial — partially apply a function by binding its leading arguments.
--- fn.when — apply a transform when a predicate holds, otherwise return the value unchanged.
--- fn.unless — apply a transform unless a predicate holds, otherwise return the value unchanged.
--- fn.converge — apply branches to a value, then combine the results with a combiner.
cap "combinators.pipe"
cap "combinators.flow"
cap "combinators.compose"
cap "combinators.fanout"
cap "combinators.fanout_fn"
cap "combinators.choice"
cap "combinators.apply"
